From 2776759697898314c009a339f322d8ae9550d14e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:18:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/17] invariant: params are hashed and travel with every run

Six param files from the SUBSTRATE values, all carrying params_version, which
must agree across the set. hash_params_dir is content-addressed so the same
configuration hashes the same on any machine. require() refuses a null value
rather than defaulting: SUBSTRATE forbids inventing thresholds, so an unset
ceiling makes the caller stop.
---
